# Project Rules: ShieldPM 4.x

## Project Overview

ShieldPM (Shedowe's Shield Proxy Manager) is an advanced fork of Nginx Proxy Manager.
It provides a web UI for managing Nginx Reverse Proxies with emphasis on security (WAF, IPS),
modern protocols (HTTP/3, QUIC), and native performance.

**Primary outputs**: Docker Image (`ghcr.io/shedowe19/shieldpm:develop`), Native Installer (`install.sh`), and LXC container deployments (via the same installer).

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| **Backend Runtime** | Node.js 24 LTS via signed NodeSource APT (ESM modules) |
| **Backend Framework** | Express.js `v5.2` |
| **ORM** | Objection.js `v3.1` / Knex.js `v3.1` |
| **Database (Dev)** | SQLite (`better-sqlite3`) |
| **Database (Prod)** | MySQL (`mysql2`) or PostgreSQL (`pg`) |
| **Frontend Framework** | React `v19.2` (TypeScript) |
| **Build Tool** | Vite `v7.3` |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS `v3.4`, shadcn/ui (Radix UI) |
| **State Management** | React Query `v5.90` |
| **i18n** | i18next / react-i18next |
| **Linter/Formatter** | Biome `v2.4` (both frontend & backend) |
| **Tests** | Vitest `v4.0` (both frontend & backend) |
| **Web Server** | OpenResty-based custom Nginx |
| **Package Manager** | Corepack + repository-pinned Yarn 4 (immutable lockfiles) |

## Architecture

### Repository Structure

```
ShieldPM/
├── backend/                # Express.js API (ESM)
│   ├── internal/           # Business logic services (singleton objects)
│   ├── models/             # Objection.js ORM models
│   ├── routes/             # Express route handlers
│   ├── schema/             # JSON Schema / API validation
│   ├── templates/          # EJS templates for Nginx configs
│   ├── migrations/         # Knex.js database migrations
│   ├── lib/                # Shared utilities (error, encryption, helpers)
│   └── app.js              # Express app setup
├── frontend/               # React SPA (TypeScript)
│   └── src/
│       ├── api/            # API client hooks (React Query)
│       ├── components/     # Reusable UI components (shadcn/ui)
│       ├── context/        # React context (auth, theme)
│       ├── hooks/          # Custom React hooks
│       ├── locale/         # i18n translation files
│       ├── modals/         # Modal dialog components
│       ├── pages/          # Route-level page components
│       └── Router.tsx      # App routing (react-router-dom)
├── rootfs/                 # Docker overlay files (startup scripts)
├── scripts/                # install.sh for native deployments
├── docs/                   # Project documentation
└── Dockerfile              # Multi-stage build
```

### Component Responsibilities

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `backend/internal/nginx.js` | **Config Engine**: Reads DB → renders EJS templates → writes `.conf` → reloads Nginx |
| `backend/internal/proxy-host.js` | CRUD + enable/disable logic for proxy hosts |
| `backend/internal/ai/` | AI integration (Gemini, Ollama, OpenAI-compatible) |
| `backend/internal/chat.js` | Telegram ChatOps bot (Telegraf) |
| `backend/internal/gitops.js` | GitOps config sync via isomorphic-git |
| `backend/internal/tor.js` | Tor Hidden Service management |
| `backend/templates/*.conf` | EJS templates defining Nginx vhost configurations |
| `rootfs/usr/local/bin/` | Container startup scripts (`launch.sh`, `start.sh`) |
| `scripts/install.sh` | Bash installer for **LXC containers** and bare-metal (native) deployments |

### Two-Repository Model

> **CRITICAL**: This app spans TWO repos. Never confuse them.

- **`ShieldPM`** (this repo) — Application source code (backend, frontend, migrations, installer). Supports **Docker**, **LXC**, and **native** deployments.
- **`shieldpm-nginx`** (external) — Base Docker image + compiled Nginx binaries. Changes to Nginx modules, compilation flags, or the root `nginx.conf` go there.

## Coding Standards

### Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| JS Variables/Functions | `camelCase` | `proxyHost`, `getAll` |
| DB Columns | `snake_case` | `owner_user_id`, `ssl_forced` |
| DB Tables | `snake_case` | `proxy_host`, `access_list` |
| React Components | `PascalCase` | `ProxyHosts`, `SiteHeader` |
| React Files | `PascalCase.tsx` | `Dashboard.tsx`, `Router.tsx` |
| CSS Classes | Tailwind utility classes | `flex flex-col min-h-screen` |
| Migration Files | `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.js` | `20260101120000_add_anubis.js` |
| Locale Keys | `dot.separated.camelCase` | `proxy.host.create` |

### Code Style (Biome)

- **Indent**: Tabs, width 4
- **Line width**: 120 characters max
- **Quotes**: Double quotes (`"`) for JS/TS strings
- **Semicolons**: Required
- **Imports**: Organized by Biome groups (node → npm → local)
- **Self-closing elements**: Required for empty JSX tags
- **No parameter reassign**: Error

### Module System

- **Backend**: ESM (`"type": "module"` in package.json). Use `import/export`, never `require()`.
- **Frontend**: ESM + TypeScript with Vite path aliases (`src/...`).
- **Migrations**: ESM with named `up`/`down` exports.
- **Exception**: Files ending in `.cjs` (e.g., `validate-env.cjs`) may use CommonJS.

### Error Handling

Backend errors use a centralized error factory (`backend/lib/error.js`):

```javascript
import errs from "../lib/error.js";

// Throw structured errors with HTTP status mapping
throw new errs.ItemNotFoundError(id);
throw new errs.AuthError("Invalid credentials");
throw new errs.PermissionError("Not allowed");
```

- Always use the `errs` factory — never throw raw `Error` objects in route/internal code.
- Let Express error middleware handle response formatting.

### Async Patterns

- **Backend**: Use `async/await` with try/catch. Return Promises from service methods.
- **Frontend**: Use React Query (`useQuery`, `useMutation`) for all API calls. Never use raw `fetch` in components.
- **Nginx operations**: Are async with debounced reload (2s delay) to avoid CPU spikes.

### Database Patterns (Objection.js)

- Models extend `Model` from Objection.js and define `tableName`, `jsonAttributes`, and `relationMappings`.
- Boolean fields are stored as integers in SQLite; models handle conversion via `convertBoolFieldsToInt`/`convertIntFieldsToBool` helpers.
- Always use `$beforeInsert` and `$beforeUpdate` lifecycle hooks for timestamps.
- Soft-delete pattern: Set `is_deleted = 1`, filter in relation `modify()` callbacks.

### Backend Service Pattern

Business logic lives in `backend/internal/` as **singleton objects** (not classes):

```javascript
const internalProxyHost = {
    create(access, data) { /* ... */ },
    update(access, data) { /* ... */ },
    get(access, data) { /* ... */ },
    delete(access, data) { /* ... */ },
    getAll(access, expand, search_query) { /* ... */ },
};
export default internalProxyHost;
```

- First parameter is always `access` (contains user identity + permissions).
- Services call other services (e.g., `internalNginx.configure()`) — never reach into DB directly from routes.

### Frontend Patterns

- **Lazy loading**: All page components use `React.lazy()` with `<Suspense>`.
- **Animations**: Use `framer-motion` `<AnimatePresence>` for page transitions.
- **Forms**: Mix of Formik and React Hook Form (+ Zod for validation). New forms should prefer React Hook Form + Zod.
- **UI Components**: Use shadcn/ui primitives (Radix-based). Do not introduce new UI libraries.
- **Icons**: Use `@tabler/icons-react` and `lucide-react`. Do not add other icon libraries.

## Critical Rules

1. ❌ **Never use `require()`** in backend code — the project is ESM-only.
2. ❌ **Never modify Nginx compilation flags** in this repo — that belongs to `shieldpm-nginx`.
3. ❌ **Never throw raw `Error` objects** in backend internal/route code — use `errs` factory.
4. ❌ **Never use raw `fetch`** in React components — use React Query hooks.
5. ❌ **Never store dynamic data outside `/data/`** — all persistent state must reside there.
6. ❌ **Never skip `$beforeInsert`/`$beforeUpdate`** lifecycle hooks when creating Objection models.
7. ✅ **Always validate with JSON Schema** before accepting API input (see `backend/schema/`).
8. ✅ **Always debounce Nginx reloads** — never call `nginx -s reload` directly; use `internalNginx.reload()`.
9. ✅ **Always use `access` parameter** as the first argument in internal service methods.
10. ✅ **Always add translations** for new UI text in `frontend/src/locale/lang/en.json` at minimum.

## Code Smells to Avoid

- **God functions**: Break services into focused methods; the `create` method should not exceed ~100 lines.
- **Inline SQL**: Always go through Objection.js query builder, not raw Knex queries (unless migration).
- **Hardcoded paths**: Use path constants or environment variables, never hardcode `/data/nginx/...`.
- **Unused imports**: Biome will flag these — fix before committing.
- **Mixed boolean types**: DB uses `0/1` integers for booleans. The model layer handles conversion. Do not mix `true/false` and `0/1` outside models.

## Testing Guidelines

- **Framework**: Vitest (both backend and frontend).
- **Frontend tests**: Use Testing Library (`@testing-library/react`).
- **Run tests**: `cd backend && yarn test` / `cd frontend && yarn test`.
- **Coverage**: Focus on service logic (`backend/internal/`) and complex UI interactions.
- **Mocking**: Mock external dependencies (Docker, Nginx, Tor, Telegram) — never hit real services in tests.

## Documentation Standards

- Use JSDoc `@param` and `@returns` comments on all backend service methods (see `proxy-host.js` for pattern).
- Use `/** @type {Type} */` annotations for model field types.
- Keep `GEMINI.md` up to date — it is the source of truth for AI agents.

## Security Considerations

- **JWT tokens**: Browser/API sessions are managed via `backend/internal/token.js` and server-side refresh sessions.
- **ChatOps principal**: Telegram requests use a live server-side integration principal bound to integration, owner and
  external user; ChatOps must never synthesize a JWT or elevate permissions.
- **CSRF**: Enabled via `csrf-csrf` middleware.
- **Rate limiting**: Applied via `express-rate-limit`.
- **Helmet**: Security headers enabled globally.
- **Encryption**: Use `backend/lib/encryption.js` for sensitive field storage (passwords, keys).
- **WAF layers**: ModSecurity (CRS v4), OpenAppSec (AI WAF), CrowdSec (IPS via Lua). Integration changes require coordination with `shieldpm-nginx`.

## Versioning

- **Source of truth**: `backend/package.json` + `frontend/package.json` + `.version` (root).
- When bumping version: update all three files, then tag the git commit.
- Always discuss Patch/Minor/Major impact with the user before bumping.
